pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Positive-direction companion of `incorrect/enumeration_after_soli`: having an
% objective, and logging a solution with a plain `sol`, must not trip the guard.
% Only `soli`/`obji` store the objective-improving constraint that removes
% solutions without counting them; `sol` removes nothing. Both projections onto
% the preserved variable x1 are witnessed and counted, so the enumeration really
% is complete.
f 1;
sol x1 ~x2;
solx x1 ~x2;
solx ~x1 x2;
pol 2 3 +;
output NONE;
conclusion ENUMERATION_COMPLETE 2;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
